'''''Lathyrus setifolius''''', the '''brown vetchling''', is a species of annual herb in the family [[Fabaceae]]. They have a self-supporting growth form and compound, broad leaves. Individuals can grow to 31&nbsp;cm.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Lathyrus setifolius L. - Encyclopedia of Life |url=https://eol.org/pages/703185 |access-date=2022-02-04 |website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mifsud |first=Stephen |date=2002-08-23 |title=Lathyrus setifolius (Red Pea) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands. |url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/FABC/Lathyrus_setifolius.php |access-date=2022-03-05 |website=www.maltawildplants.com |language=en-us}}</ref>

